# graphify's detect() respects .gitignore by default. ProductionStudio/Cases/*/ is
# gitignored (decided 2026-08-15 — case content isn't tracked in git anymore) on the
# explicit premise that it's still indexed locally by graphify. Without this negation,
# graphify silently skips every case's production docs, which is exactly the kind of
# stale-graph failure CLAUDE.md warns about (the Monica Sementilli incident) — discovered
# 2026-08-15 while running graphify for the Yolanda Marodi case, when detect() came back
# with zero files under Cases/ at all. Re-include it here, for graphify only; git tracking
# is unaffected.
!ProductionStudio/Cases/*/
